\ Fast regressions for lexicographically ordered cutlet name sequences.
\ The names are distinct and chosen without replacement from 1..17.
\ These tests use exact ranks rather than the slow Foundation sauce.

To check the count of cutlet name sequences:
  Put 1 into the selected cutlet count.
  Count all cutlet name sequences.
  If the cutlet name choice's total sequences is not "17",
    put "One cutlet should have seventeen possible names." into the check report; exit.
  Put 3 into the selected cutlet count.
  Count all cutlet name sequences.
  If the cutlet name choice's total sequences is not "4080",
    put "Three cutlets should have 4080 distinct name sequences." into the check report; exit.
  Put 17 into the selected cutlet count.
  Count all cutlet name sequences.
  If the cutlet name choice's total sequences is not "355687428096000",
    put "The seventeen-name permutation count is not 17 factorial." into the check report; exit.

To verify three cutlet name indices given a number and another number and a third number:
  Put the chosen cutlet names' first into the examined cutlet name assignment.
  If the examined cutlet name assignment is nil,
    put "The first cutlet name was missing." into the check report; exit.
  If the examined cutlet name assignment's name index is not the number,
    put "The first cutlet name index differs from its reference." into the check report; exit.
  Put the examined cutlet name assignment's next into the examined cutlet name assignment.
  If the examined cutlet name assignment is nil,
    put "The second cutlet name was missing." into the check report; exit.
  If the examined cutlet name assignment's name index is not the other number,
    put "The second cutlet name index differs from its reference." into the check report; exit.
  Put the examined cutlet name assignment's next into the examined cutlet name assignment.
  If the examined cutlet name assignment is nil,
    put "The third cutlet name was missing." into the check report; exit.
  If the examined cutlet name assignment's name index is not the third number,
    put "The third cutlet name index differs from its reference." into the check report; exit.
  If the examined cutlet name assignment's next is not nil,
    put "A three-cutlet name list includes extra names." into the check report; exit.

To check lexicographic cutlet names:
  Put 3 into the selected cutlet count.
  Put "1" into a name rank wide quantity.
  Select cutlet names from the name rank wide quantity.
  If the cutlet name choice's selection success is not 1,
    put "First name sequence was not selected." into the check report; exit.
  Verify three cutlet name indices given 1 and 2 and 3.
  Put "15" into the name rank wide quantity.
  Select cutlet names from the name rank wide quantity.
  Verify three cutlet name indices given 1 and 2 and 17.
  Put "16" into the name rank wide quantity.
  Select cutlet names from the name rank wide quantity.
  Verify three cutlet name indices given 1 and 3 and 2.
  Put "4080" into the name rank wide quantity.
  Select cutlet names from the name rank wide quantity.
  Verify three cutlet name indices given 17 and 16 and 15.
  Put "4081" into the name rank wide quantity.
  Select cutlet names from the name rank wide quantity.
  If the cutlet name choice's selection success is not 0,
    put "An out-of-range name-sequence rank was accepted." into the check report; exit.
  Put "0" into the name rank wide quantity.
  Select cutlet names from the name rank wide quantity.
  If the cutlet name choice's selection success is not 0,
    put "Rank zero was accepted for a name sequence." into the check report; exit.
